  "_status": "TEMPLATE - every REQUIRED_* token must be replaced with a measured value before use; the six runner rejects this file unchanged and identity is NOT ready before the actual capture.",
  "_instructions": [
    "Copy to runs/tp-ep-six/startup-2rtx6-tp6ep1.json and replace every REQUIRED_* token.",
    "Pure TP6EP1 is ONE unreplicated group: the Spark image must additionally advertise the spark_tp6 role (tp_degree 6, intermediate 384, no storage padding). A library that only carries roles 1/5/6 cannot serve this arm.",
    "expert_tp_manifests is a superset rule against the baseline arm: every baseline family must be present with an equal native_library_sha256, and the candidate adds the spark_tp6 family its role selects.",
    "Launch the isolated candidate process (coordinator 127.0.0.1:18000, expert 0.0.0.0:29441) from the staged candidate bytes; do NOT use the release run.sh defaults (port 8000 / default services).",
    "Budget: 109119320064 B per Spark host is the global minimum-of-six. Pure TP6 needs 40 * 1,203,240,960 = 48,129,638,400 B per rank for all 40 remote layers, so 20 remote layers need 24,064,819,200 B.",
    "The moa coordinator peer address 10.55.0.12 is PROVISIONAL pending the select_rc_gid/device/HCA/rail review plus a live RC probe; the ip-route-B observation alone does not prove a matched RoCE path.",
    "worker_runtime_role must be the readiness line each rank actually logged: role 7 (spark_tp6), intermediate 384, world 6, with the source log per rank. A manifest advertises an artifact; it does not prove the running rank loaded that role.",
    "requested_adaptive_cost_mode is the operator's DS41RT_ADAPTIVE_COST_MODE value; resolved_cost_model is the `cost_model=` label the coordinator actually logged. Record both, because auto resolves differently per layout and a cross-topology A/B under two models is confounded."
  ],
